{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-38703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} & -2\\end{aligned}],$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-38703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{5} \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-38703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15cb6b92d182e5278ecaaaa3821a9a850fd84daaabbb087c401a2c99368d7107"} {"question" "q-38703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-38703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{9}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-38703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{9}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-85921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-85921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\sqrt{2})\\cdot 2-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =-7\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-85921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15cb6b92d182e5278ecaaaa3821a9a850fd84daaabbb087c401a2c99368d7107"} {"question" "q-85921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-85921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "-4\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "-7\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-85921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83391" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}],$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83391" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot 7-(-5)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-28+15 \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83391" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15cb6b92d182e5278ecaaaa3821a9a850fd84daaabbb087c401a2c99368d7107"} {"question" "q-83391" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83391" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-13"] ["math" "-18"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "43"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83391" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-13"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}],$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =10-24 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15cb6b92d182e5278ecaaaa3821a9a850fd84daaabbb087c401a2c99368d7107"} {"question" "q-83393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-14"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "34"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-14"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{aligned}],$ find the sum of the eigenvalues of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the trace of $A.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A)=5-6=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15cb6b92d182e5278ecaaaa3821a9a850fd84daaabbb087c401a2c99368d7107"} {"question" "q-83390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-83390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-140522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix with the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )=-{\\lambda }^{3}+5\\lambda -7.$ Then, ${A}^{3}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-140522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ -{A}^{3}+5A-7I & =O \\\\ {A}^{3} & =5A-7I.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "96a13739d7a610dc9cb395580389e4bd325188e2a3db4bd945101b73359b7104"} {"question" "q-140522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15cb6b92d182e5278ecaaaa3821a9a850fd84daaabbb087c401a2c99368d7107"} {"question" "q-140522" "field" "selection" "attri